%I A399035 #32 Oct 17 2026 16:10:28
%S A399035 1,0,0,1,0,4,7,34,128,587,2838,14884,83369,496948,3136332,20874825,
%T A399035 146013340,1070057040,8194014727,65406783310,543069224812,
%U A399035 4681196972123,41818695066314,386551229052000,3691794585277009,36381865455478328,369503343798571624
%N A399035 The unique sequence a(n) such that A000296(n) = a(n) + a(n+1).
%C A399035 The usual "1+Shift" operator modified so that 1 + blank is omitted rather than replaced by 1, for agreement with how Peirce laid out the diagonals of his table in his 1880 paper Algebra of Logic.
%C A399035 There does not exist a sequence of nonnegative integers whose 1+Shift transform is this sequence. Hence, in the infinite chain of sequences obtained by repeatedly applying the 1+Shift operator (the "Peirce sequences"), this is the first member. The sequences A000296, A000110, A011968, A011969, and A011970, shortened in the manner used by Peirce when laying out his diagonals in his 1880 paper "Algebra of Logic", also as in Quaintance & Kwong, 2013 which includes A000296, are the next five, and in principle the process can be continued indefinitely.
%D A399035 C. S. Peirce, On the Algebra of Logic, American Journal of Mathematics 3 (1), 15-57 (March 1880).
%D A399035 Jocelyn Quaintance and Harris Kwong, A combinatorial interpretation of the Catalan and Bell number difference tables, INTEGERS 13 (2013), #A29.
%H A399035 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A399035/b399035.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..500</a>
%F A399035 a(0) = 1, a(n+1) = A000296(n) - a(n).
%F A399035 G.f.: If B(x) is the g.f. of A000296 as shortened, then A(x) = B(x) / (1 + x).
%e A399035 A000296 begins 1,0,1,1,4,11,41,162,... , so we have:
%e A399035 a(0) = 1, a(1) = 1 - 1 = 0, a(2) = 0 - 0 - 0, a(3) = 1 - 1 = 0,
%e A399035 a(4) = 4 - 0 = 4, etc.
%t A399035 FoldList[#2 - # &, 1, FoldList[BellB[#2] - # &, 1, Range[0, 25]]] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 17 2026 *)
%t A399035 (* Alternative: *)
%t A399035 Module[{a, n}, RecurrenceTable[{a[n] == BellB[n - 2] - 2*a[n - 1] - a[n - 2], a[0] == 1, a[1] == 0}, a, {n, 0, 27}]] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 17 2026 *)
%Y A399035 Cf. A000296 (1+Shift of this sequence). Cf. also A000110, A011968, A011969, A011970 (beheaded to give corresponding Peirce sequences).
%K A399035 nonn,new
%O A399035 0,6
%A A399035 _Vaughan R Pratt_, Oct 16 2026
